Subject: "Discard your hand, then draw N": cast it only when the hand is nearly empty
Why: DiscardAi.checkApiLogic has a comment for spells that make the AI discard its own hand
  ("the ai should only be using something like this if he has few cards in hand") but no check,
  so Stoke Genius (the adventure of Hearth Elemental, Izzet Spellementals: {1}{R}, discard your
  hand, then draw two cards) was cast whenever the mana was there. In a 30-games-per-pairing
  gauntlet of Izzet Spellementals against the meta decks (seed 1, --save-logs) 219 of its 249
  casts discarded three or more cards, most often five, for two. Now, for Mode$ Hand defined as
  the AI itself with Draw sub-abilities, the spell is cast only if it throws away fewer cards
  than it draws, counting nonland cards, and lands too once five are on the battlefield.
  The same rule applies to Dangerous Wager, Change of Fortune, Contract from Below and Blood
  for the Blood God.
Measured: `mtgsim gauntlet decks/standard/meta/izzet-spellementals.txt --vs <the other 17 meta
  decks> -n 100 --seed 1`, default AI, Forge 7db198d72e, on 16 Nov 2026, both arms built on
  0001-0011 plus a candidate 0012 that was later dropped (it touches only Umbral Collar Zealot
  sacrifices). Without this patch: 32.9% (95% CI 31-35%, 560-1140). With it: 36.2% (34-39%,
  616-1084). Difference +3.3 points, 95% CI +0.1 to +6.5 (paired over the same 1,700 seeds:
  +1.6 to +5.0; 136 losses became wins, 80 wins became losses). Casts of the Hearth Elemental
  card (both halves) fell from 2,951 to 2,169. Mirror with the patch (`match izzet-spellementals
  izzet-spellementals -n 200 --seed 1`): 51.0% (44-58%).

